 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? That's very common problem. It's usually because you drawing the nose from a side view, and human faces don't actually look like that. That's about right. We' going for a flat, two-dimensional drawing, so the eyes should be level with the top of the head, and the opening is about the width of a pencil. Try drawing the other features first, like the head, cheeks and mouth. Then draw the nose, starting from the sides of the mouth. It usually looks better when it's separate. That's the way. Draw for five minutes, start to finish, and pick something fun. You' be surprised how much you remember.",
